2540, "displayName": "NF-kB is sequestered in the cytosol of unstimulated cells th...", "text": "NF-kB is sequestered in the cytosol of unstimulated cells through the interactions with a class of inhibitor proteins, called IkBs, which mask the nuclear localization signal (NLS) of NF-kB and prevent its nuclear translocation. A key event in NF-kB activation involves phosphorylation of IkB (at sites equivalent to Ser32 and Ser36 of IkB-alpha or Ser19 and Ser22 of IkB-beta) by IKK. The phosphorylated IkB-alpha is recognized by the E3 ligase complex and targeted for ubiquitin-mediated proteasomal degradation, releasing the NF-kB dimer p50/p65 into the nucleus to turn on target genes. (Karin & Ben-Neriah 2000)", "literatureReference": [{"dbId": 2685476, "displayName": "Phosphorylation meets ubiquitination: the control of NF-[kappa]B activity", "title": "Phosphorylation meets ubiquitination: the control of NF-[kappa]B activity", "journal": "Annu. Rev. Immunol.", "pages": "621-63", "pubMedIdentifier": 10837071, "volume": 18, "year": 2000, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10837071", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}], "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "updateTrackers": [{"dbId": 9787446, "displayName": "Update Tracker - [Reaction:202541] p-S177,S181-IKKB:IKKA:pUb-NEMO phosphorylates IkB-alpha:NF-kB - v45:[add_removeOutput]", "action": ["add_removeOutput"], "updatedInstance": [202541], "className": "UpdateTracker", "schemaClass": "UpdateTracker"}, {"dbId": 9786324, "displayName": "Update Tracker - [Reaction:202541] p-S177,S181-IKKB:IKKA:pUb-NEMO phosphorylates IkB-alpha:NF-kB - v50:[add_removeOutput]", "action": ["add_removeOutput"], "updatedInstance": [202541], "className": "UpdateTracker", "schemaClass": "UpdateTracker"},